Description: pkg itself comes only from NextBSD
 For pkg and pkg-devel, drop any remote candidate whose repository is not
 "NextBSD", wherever libpkg's job universe collects remote candidates, so no
 other repository can install or upgrade pkg. And refuse to install or
 replace pkg or pkg-devel from a local package file (pkg add, pkg install
 ./file.pkg) unless the package is a NextBSD package: its manifest carries
 the annotation org.nextbsd.origin=NextBSD, which nextbsd-pkg stamps on
 every package it builds. Everything else in pkg behaves as upstream.
 .
 Repositories: the design names pkg_jobs_universe_get_remote() as the one
 place. In 2.8.4 that function serves only dependency resolution: the
 self-upgrade check (new_pkg_version() -> pkg_jobs_find_upgrade() ->
 pkg_jobs_process_remote_pkg()), pkg install and pkg upgrade collect their
 candidates in pkg_jobs_universe_get_upgrade_candidates(), and shlib and
 provide lookups in pkg_jobs_universe_handle_provide(). The same filter is
 applied in all three loops so the rule holds on every path.
 .
 Package files (added by the maintainer after the design): the check is
 nextbsd_check_install() in the new libpkg/nextbsd_policy.c. It runs from
 pkg_jobs_execute() over every package a job is about to install
 (nextbsd_check_jobs(), before anything is extracted, so the whole
 transaction is refused), and from pkg_add_common() for each package pkg add
 installs, before its dependencies are added or anything is extracted.
Origin: NextBSD, https://github.com/nextbsd/nextbsd-pkg/wiki/NextBSD-pkg-only-from-NextBSD (design section 1)
Bug: https://github.com/nextbsd/nextbsd-contrib/issues/7
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-25
---
--- a/libpkg/pkg_jobs_universe.c
+++ b/libpkg/pkg_jobs_universe.c
@@ -108,6 +108,33 @@
 	return (pkg);
 }
 
+/*
+ * NextBSD: pkg itself comes only from the NextBSD repository.
+ *
+ * A remote pkg or pkg-devel from any other repository is never a candidate,
+ * so no other repository can install or upgrade pkg: not the self-upgrade
+ * check (new_pkg_version()), pkg upgrade, pkg install, pkg install -r <repo>,
+ * dependency resolution, nor a shlib or provide lookup.  The repository name
+ * is fixed.  Local packages and package files (pkg add) are not affected.
+ */
+#define	NEXTBSD_PKG_REPO	"NextBSD"
+
+static bool
+nextbsd_foreign_pkg(const struct pkg *pkg)
+{
+	if (pkg->type != PKG_REMOTE)
+		return (false);
+	if (!STREQ(pkg->name, "pkg") && !STREQ(pkg->name, "pkg-devel"))
+		return (false);
+	if (pkg->reponame != NULL && STREQ(pkg->reponame, NEXTBSD_PKG_REPO))
+		return (false);
+	dbg(1, "NextBSD: ignoring %s-%s from repository %s: "
+	    "pkg comes only from the " NEXTBSD_PKG_REPO " repository",
+	    pkg->name, pkg->version,
+	    pkg->reponame != NULL ? pkg->reponame : "(none)");
+	return (true);
+}
